<title>PORTUGAL: Adtrantz/Siemens win Portuguese deal.</title>
<headline>Adtrantz/Siemens win Portuguese deal.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lisbon underground railway company Metropolitano de Lisboa has ordered 54 carriages from a consortium including Adtranz Portugal and Siemens in a deal worth 15.5 billion escudos, the consortium said.</p>
<p>Adtranz is a joint venture between Daimler-Benz and ABB.</p>
<p>The first carriage will be delivered in July 1998 and the order should be completed in April 1999, a statement said.</p>
<p>The latest order complements a March 1995 order from Metropolitana de Lisboa for 114 carriages from the consortium.</p>
<p>Adtranz Portugal, a unit of Adtranz, is responsible for 60 percent of the new order and Siemens the remaining 40 percent.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
